  "summary": {
    "title": "Meade CPA Plaid Integration Threat Model",
    "owner": "Toshi Troyer",
    "description": "An internal, staff-facing web application for Meade CPA, an accounting and tax firm. Staff use it to connect client bank accounts via Plaid (transactions, holdings, liabilities), upload and manage client documents, and export the resulting financial data. No client ever logs into this application directly; the only client-facing touchpoint is a one-time Plaid Hosted Link session used to connect a bank account, completed outside this app's own sessions. The frontend is a React app served by Azure Static Web Apps; the backend is a set of Azure Functions handling API requests and Plaid webhooks. Client and financial data is stored in Azure SQL; uploaded documents and generated exports are stored in Azure Blob Storage. TaxDome is the firm's system of record for client documents and data; the current handoff from this application to TaxDome is manual, staff download an export and upload it directly, since TaxDome's API is not yet available for automated integration.",
    "id": 0
  },
